# Independent Notes inline-confirmation review

Acceptance is withheld for one finite Cancel-policy failure. Opening a saved note, opening notebook Trash/Restore confirmation, and cancelling causes a new `attachment-list` read. `organize` restores controls and calls `accept(current)` in its `finally` block; after its busy gate clears, that call launches the read. The frozen candidate documentation promises no follow-up reads on Cancel. The independent model and an actual owned Chrome/HTTP run both reproduce the request. No notebook mutation, saved note change, or draft loss was demonstrated.

The nine author fresh test bodies replayed with imports-only adapters and passed. Seven independent groups cover reopened questions and retained old buttons, child notebook selection, pending Restore duplication/keyboard input, disposal during each post-commit get/list/notebook-list await, rejected persistence after disposal, and active-note cancellation. The initial 16-group run was14pass/2fail. One failure incorrectly required active `deleted_time` to be explicitly `0` rather than omitted; its exact source/raw remains here. Correcting only that fixture assertion yields15pass/1fail. The genuine no-follow-up-read assertion is unchanged. Both runs authenticated candidate215 artifacts including its manifest, current production28, and retained original-source31 before/after.

The owned Chrome run used the exact candidate Notes runtime and shared host, plus three separately authenticated current public shell files. It proved actual in-page Confirm/Cancel, initial Cancel focus, Tab and Shift+Tab, Escape and Space cancellation, Enter confirmation, recursive notebook Trash/Restore, dirty-draft refusal, saving and reopening revision4, and navigation disposal of an unanswered question. Browser observations confirm one Trash and one Restore request, and one extra attachment-list request on the first active-note cancellation. Browser response delays were not injected; disposal after held committed/read responses was exercised by the real component/backend model tests. Assistive technology, original Joplin GUI/database, and benchmarks were not executed.

The private host was port63121 with synthetic temporary data only; it exited0 after explicit close. The owned tab closed successfully. Confined temporary data was removed after the host drained. User4311 was untouched. The private deployment deliberately contains only Notes: navigation to Lab Editor exercised unchanged shell cleanup and produced the expected absent-module message, retained as a harness boundary, not an Editor failure. Screenshots, AX states, request records, source copies, and cleanup are retained under `browser/`.

The immutable214 author stage, its preparation/finalizer failures and source-paired harness adaptations remain intact. Its accepted historical325/37/504/61 epochs and focused149 evidence of138 tests were fully authenticated separately after the campaign; their manifest/reference identities were already pinned in candidate214 before the campaign. No historical result is rebound to candidate bytes. Original Joplin3.6.14 source/license/provenance bytes are authenticated from the existing31-file ledger; this review executes no original helpers. Root owns a future separate runtime correction and installation. Production, requirements, shared code, and all earlier evidence were unchanged by this review.
